WEBVTT

00:01:28.951 --> 00:01:31.260
Where do I want the conversation
to go from here,

00:01:31.284 --> 00:01:32.441
if anywhere at all?

00:01:32.465 --> 00:01:33.861
And how do I want this person

00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:36.853
to understand my own relationship
with this aspect of who I am?

00:01:36.877 --> 00:01:39.516
So, in my case, I knew
I wanted people to call me

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.466
by my new name and pronouns.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:43.566
But I also didn't want them to avoid me

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.097
out of fear of messing them up.

00:01:45.121 --> 00:01:46.470
This was going to take time.

00:01:46.494 --> 00:01:49.226
And I wanted this to feel
like any other ordinary fact

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.776
about who I am.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:52.852
So now we know what we want
to communicate.

00:01:52.876 --> 00:01:54.937
Let's talk about how
we're going to say it.

00:01:54.961 --> 00:01:56.191
By setting the tone.

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:58.437
You're going to want
to present the information

00:01:58.461 --> 00:02:00.754
in the same way you want
people to respond to it.